# macOS Finder droppings. They change constantly and would make the watcher
# commit noise all day, which is exactly how a busy channel starts looking like
# a broken one.
.DS_Store
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes

# THE ROOT HEARTBEAT, untracked from S063 and this is the fix for a dead road.
#
# Both machines wrote and committed this one file every two minutes. Two
# divergent commits on the same single line, every cycle, which guarantees a
# rebase conflict rather than risking one, and both machines were found wedged
# mid-rebase because of it.
#
# It is still WRITTEN every cycle on every machine, because Code's session-open
# hook reads its timestamp off its own disk to answer "did my watcher run". It
# simply never needed to travel to answer that. Cross-machine liveness moved to
# heartbeat/<machine>.txt, one path per machine, where a conflict is impossible.
HEARTBEAT.txt

# Editor and temporary files, so a half-saved document never travels as though
# it were a delivered instruction.
*.swp
*~
.~lock.*
